{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-39943","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63570","text":"Slice B, Commit 3 — the "},{"id":"spn-63571","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63572","text":" surface: closure memo"}]},{"id":"blk-39944","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63573","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-63574","text":" CLOSED. "},{"id":"spn-63575","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run48"},{"id":"spn-63576","text":" PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (6s, 71 rows). "},{"id":"spn-63577","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate48"},{"id":"spn-63578","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63579","marks":["bold"],"text":"19/19 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-63580","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-63581","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-63582","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63583","marks":["bold"],"text":"16/16 green"},{"id":"spn-63584","text":" (141s, reference + native), L-0 tier unmoved."}]},{"id":"blk-39945","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63585","text":"Commit 2 gave a route a canonical form and an identity but no spelling. Commit 3 gives it the ruled spelling in both directions:"}]},{"id":"blk-39946","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7)"},{"id":"blk-39947","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63586","text":"and closes the two things that spelling makes reachable — the Q4 writer-15 reservation, and a silent world substitution in the authoring draft."}]},{"id":"blk-39948","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63587","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39950","spans":[{"id":"spn-63588","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-39951","spans":[{"id":"spn-63589","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-39949","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39952","spans":[{"id":"spn-63590","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39953","spans":[{"id":"spn-63591","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_RE"},{"id":"spn-63592","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63593","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_KEYS"},{"id":"spn-63594","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63595","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-63596","text":", the route branch in "},{"id":"spn-63597","marks":["code"],"text":"_parse_core_permissive"},{"id":"spn-63598","text":"; bootstrap "},{"id":"spn-63599","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63600","text":" message split off from "},{"id":"spn-63601","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-63602","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63603","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]}],[{"id":"blk-39954","spans":[{"id":"spn-63604","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39955","spans":[{"id":"spn-63605","text":"route section emitted after the edges, "},{"id":"spn-63606","marks":["code"],"text":"_emit_body"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39956","spans":[{"id":"spn-63607","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39957","spans":[{"id":"spn-63608","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ROUTE_WRITER_RESERVED"},{"id":"spn-63609","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63610","marks":["code"],"text":"routes_of_artifact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39958","spans":[{"id":"spn-63611","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39959","spans":[{"id":"spn-63612","marks":["code"],"text":"check_route_writer_reservation"},{"id":"spn-63613","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63614","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39960","spans":[{"id":"spn-63615","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39961","spans":[{"id":"spn-63616","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-63617","text":", the computed "},{"id":"spn-63618","marks":["code"],"text":"_draft_loss"},{"id":"spn-63619","text":" round-trip, both draft doors"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39962","spans":[{"id":"spn-63620","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39963","spans":[{"id":"spn-63621","text":"call site widened to the composed door"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39964","spans":[{"id":"spn-63622","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39965","spans":[{"id":"spn-63623","text":"closing NOTE corrected (it said \"there is no "},{"id":"spn-63624","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63625","text":" surface\")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-39966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63626","text":"The parser's job stops at "},{"id":"spn-63627","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"this line says a route.\""},{"id":"spn-63628","text":" Endpoint roles, the one-shot source law, the body range, duplicates and the budget are all the seal's, and they are the seal's for a route arriving from "},{"id":"spn-63629","marks":["bold"],"text":"any"},{"id":"spn-63630","text":" surface. Every Q7 row proves this twice: the parse "},{"id":"spn-63631","marks":["bold"],"text":"succeeds"},{"id":"spn-63632","text":" and the seal "},{"id":"spn-63633","marks":["bold"],"text":"refuses"},{"id":"spn-63634","text":". A parser that had helpfully re-implemented one of these fails the first half."}]},{"id":"blk-39967","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63635","text":"2. Five autonomous decisions — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-39968","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63636","text":"(a) The draft "},{"id":"spn-63637","marks":["bold"],"text":"REFUSES"},{"id":"spn-63638","text":" route-bearing worlds rather than being widened"}]},{"id":"blk-39969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63639","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-63640","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldDraft"},{"id":"spn-63641","text":" stores a world as "},{"id":"spn-63642","marks":["code"],"text":"(objects, edges)"},{"id":"spn-63643","text":". A route is neither, so it was invisible. "},{"id":"spn-63644","marks":["bold"],"text":"Measured before the guard was written:"},{"id":"spn-63645","text":" opening the one-route world for editing produced no error and yielded "},{"id":"spn-63646","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d3e555be…"},{"id":"spn-63647","text":" — the route-free twin, a perfectly good world with a perfectly good id. Legal, which is what makes it dangerous."}]},{"id":"blk-39970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63648","text":"Widening the draft to carry routes is not a language change: it is a new revision of "},{"id":"spn-63649","marks":["bold"],"text":"every persisted authoring document"},{"id":"spn-63650","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-63651","marks":["code"],"text":"ForgeProjectV2"},{"id":"spn-63652","text":", the v0.6-0 recovery journal, the draft-state ledger, the canvas reconciler. That is a document-format migration and it does not belong inside a language slice, so commit 3 ships a "},{"id":"spn-63653","marks":["bold"],"text":"refusal"},{"id":"spn-63654","text":" and defers the widening."}]},{"id":"blk-39971","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63655","text":"The guard is a "},{"id":"spn-63656","marks":["bold"],"text":"computed round-trip"},{"id":"spn-63657","text":", not a construct blacklist:"}]},{"id":"blk-39972","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"want = W.lower_graph(g).semantic_artifact_id\ngot, err = _seal(objects, edges, profile)\nif err is None and got == want: return None      # nothing was lost"},{"id":"blk-39973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63658","text":"It names no construct, so it will refuse the "},{"id":"spn-63659","marks":["italic"],"text":"next"},{"id":"spn-63660","text":" unrepresentable construct without being edited — the same property that made "},{"id":"spn-63661","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_legacy.export_canvas_graph_v1"},{"id":"spn-63662","text":" learn about routes on its own."}]},{"id":"blk-39974","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63663","text":"(b) The loss refusal reports "},{"id":"spn-63664","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"}]},{"id":"blk-39975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63665","marks":["code"],"text":"REPLACE_STATUS"},{"id":"spn-63666","text":" has four frozen terminal values. "},{"id":"spn-63667","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"},{"id":"spn-63668","text":" is the only one whose "},{"id":"spn-63669","marks":["bold"],"text":"behaviour"},{"id":"spn-63670","text":" is exactly this case (refused, draft untouched, nothing for the author to repair). It is an imperfect "},{"id":"spn-63671","marks":["italic"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-63672","text":"; the diagnostic carries the honest code "},{"id":"spn-63673","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-63674","text":". Inventing a fifth status is a change to a published contract, not a language decision — hence the deferral."}]},{"id":"blk-39976","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63675","text":"(c) Routes emit "},{"id":"spn-63676","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-63677","text":" the edges, not interleaved"}]},{"id":"blk-39977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63678","text":"Sorting a route into edge order would need one comparison key spanning two vocabularies, and the two orderings are canonical for different reasons: an edge's order is "},{"id":"spn-63679","marks":["bold"],"text":"presentational"},{"id":"spn-63680","text":", a route's order "},{"id":"spn-63681","marks":["bold"],"text":"IS its minted ADMIT `sequence`"},{"id":"spn-63682","text":" (Q4). Interleaving would make an identity-bearing order look like a formatting choice. A route-free world therefore emits "},{"id":"spn-63683","marks":["italic"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-63684","text":" the pre-Slice-B text — no separator, no empty section (proved by "},{"id":"spn-63685","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5d"},{"id":"spn-63686","text":", see §3)."}]},{"id":"blk-39978","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63687","text":"(d) "},{"id":"spn-63688","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"},{"id":"spn-63689","text":" composes binding + reservation into one door"}]},{"id":"blk-39979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63690","text":"Both halves stay callable by name, but production goes through the composed door, because the failure mode of two independent checks is that a call site grows one and not the other — and the forgotten half is whichever was added second. Today that is the reservation. "},{"id":"spn-63691","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8i"},{"id":"spn-63692","text":" and mutation "},{"id":"spn-63693","marks":["bold"],"text":"M16"},{"id":"spn-63694","text":" are the rows that hold this."}]},{"id":"blk-39980","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63695","text":"(e) The bootstrap DSL gets "},{"id":"spn-63696","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-63697","text":" route directive"}]},{"id":"blk-39981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63698","text":"It is a frozen migration bridge. Its "},{"id":"spn-63699","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63700","text":" rejection was corrected, though: it used to say "},{"id":"spn-63701","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a transition class, not an IR v1 edge\""},{"id":"spn-63702","text":", which is now false twice over — a route "},{"id":"spn-63703","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-63704","text":" an IR v1.1 construct, and it was never an edge (D8). It now points at the surface that does have one. "},{"id":"spn-63705","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-63706","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-63707","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-63708","text":" keep the old message. This is the identical correction commit 1 made for "},{"id":"spn-63709","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-63710","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-39982","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63711","text":"3. What the mutation round found"}]},{"id":"blk-39983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63712","text":"Three survivors on the first pass, all three real. Recorded because they are the useful part."}]},{"id":"blk-39984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63713","marks":["bold"],"text":"M9 — the route separator emitted unconditionally. SURVIVED with nothing red."},{"id":"spn-63714","text":" The most useful finding. Whitespace is non-semantic, so no identity moved and "},{"id":"spn-63715","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5"},{"id":"spn-63716","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63717","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5b"},{"id":"spn-63718","text":" stayed green. And the formatter is "},{"id":"spn-63719","marks":["code"],"text":"graph -> text"},{"id":"spn-63720","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-63721","marks":["code"],"text":"text -> text"},{"id":"spn-63722","text":", so the extra blank line is a "},{"id":"spn-63723","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed point"},{"id":"spn-63724","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-63725","marks":["code"],"text":"Q3b"},{"id":"spn-63726","text":" (idempotence) stayed green too; the prediction that it would catch this was simply wrong. Meanwhile the canonical "},{"id":"spn-63727","marks":["bold"],"text":"bytes"},{"id":"spn-63728","text":" of every route-free world in the tree had moved — the exact law "},{"id":"spn-63729","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format"},{"id":"spn-63730","text":"'s own comment claims (\"no blank separator, no empty section\") and which nothing checked. "},{"id":"spn-63731","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q5d` exists because of this line"},{"id":"spn-63732","text":", and states the law structurally (a route-free world's text ends at its last edge) rather than pinning a literal, which would fork the emitter."}]},{"id":"blk-39985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63733","marks":["bold"],"text":"M11 — `replace_world_source`'s guard removed. `Q9e` stayed green."},{"id":"spn-63734","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63735","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-63736","text":" claims \"the draft is UNTOUCHED\". True, but for the wrong reason: the route-free twin of that source "},{"id":"spn-63737","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-63738","text":" the draft's current world, so a missing guard falls through to the semantic-noop branch and leaves revision 0 with the right candidate. "},{"id":"spn-63739","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-63740","text":" is structurally unable to tell "},{"id":"spn-63741","marks":["italic"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-63742","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-63743","marks":["italic"],"text":"silently accepted as a no-op"},{"id":"spn-63744","text":". "},{"id":"spn-63745","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q9h`/`Q9i`/`Q9j` were added"},{"id":"spn-63746","text":": a paste whose lost world is a "},{"id":"spn-63747","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-63748","text":" world (two mailboxes + a route), plus a vacuity check that the twin really does differ."}]},{"id":"blk-39986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63749","marks":["bold"],"text":"M14 — the reservation widened to every world. Reported as \"Q8 raised\"."},{"id":"spn-63750","text":" Not a production defect but a reporting one: "},{"id":"spn-63751","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-63752","text":" raised, and "},{"id":"spn-63753","marks":["code"],"text":"section()"},{"id":"spn-63754","text":" renamed the failure after its neighbour — so a reservation made too "},{"id":"spn-63755","marks":["bold"],"text":"strong"},{"id":"spn-63756","text":" read as a reservation that was "},{"id":"spn-63757","marks":["bold"],"text":"broken"},{"id":"spn-63758","text":". "},{"id":"spn-63759","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-63760","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63761","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8c"},{"id":"spn-63762","text":" are callables now and keep their own names. (This is the same lesson as run47's \"many laws share one error code\": a row must be identifiable as itself when it fails.)"}]},{"id":"blk-39987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63763","text":"Also worth recording: "},{"id":"spn-63764","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-63765","text":" (body arity forked onto "},{"id":"spn-63766","marks":["code"],"text":"_rotor_dots"},{"id":"spn-63767","text":") is caught only at section granularity, and "},{"id":"spn-63768","marks":["code"],"text":"Q1d"},{"id":"spn-63769","text":" cannot see it at all — the rotor message happens to contain the same "},{"id":"spn-63770","marks":["code"],"text":"\"must have 4 lanes\""},{"id":"spn-63771","text":" while saying "},{"id":"spn-63772","marks":["italic"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-63773","text":" about a "},{"id":"spn-63774","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-63775","text":". That is exactly the drift "},{"id":"spn-63776","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-63777","text":"'s docstring refuses, and it is why the two 4s are not one constant."}]},{"id":"blk-39988","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63778","text":"4. Not frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-39989","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63779","text":"A route can now be "},{"id":"spn-63780","marks":["bold"],"text":"written, canonicalized, sealed, formatted, and refused for every reason it should be"},{"id":"spn-63781","text":" — and it still does nothing at runtime. Commit 4 folds it. Freeze the Slice B line after Commit 4, then promote "},{"id":"spn-63782","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63783","text":" to Grounded in "},{"id":"spn-63784","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-63785","text":" §14."}]},{"id":"blk-39990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63786","text":"Carried obligation into Commit 4: unify "},{"id":"spn-63787","marks":["code"],"text":"route_body_in_range"},{"id":"spn-63788","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-63789","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-63790","text":" to remove the fork (the obligation is written into the function's docstring)."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraa6l6k6ipdcctsojzr2eg6obk3atx6r2yk3wsi7emzijqmht5tq5a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}